<h1>Connect to UpToDate using your UTORid</h1>

<p><a href="https://www.uptodate.com/home"><b>UpToDate</b></a> is a licensed resource available to <b>students</b> through the University of Toronto Libraries.</p>

<p><strong><a href='/utorauth/?url=https://uptodate.com' class="loginButton">Login to UpToDate with your UTORid</a></strong>

<p><b>UpToDate</b> allows for individual account creation after login. Please refer to <b>UpToDate's</b> <a href="https://www.uptodate.com/home/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>.</p>

<h2>Trouble accessing UpToDate?</h2>
<p>Email <a href="mailto:ask.gerstein@utoronto.ca">ask.gerstein@utoronto.ca</a> with your name and UTORid so that we can assist you.

<h2>Obtain your UTORid</h2>
<p>For assistance with determining or obtaining your UTORid, please contact us at <a href='mailto:reader.reg@utoronto.ca'>reader.reg@utoronto.ca.</a> If you are eligible to obtain a UTORid, library staff will provide you with activation instructions.</p>

<h2>Reset your UTORid Password</h2>
<p>If you know your UTORid but you have forgotten your password, please contact the <a href='mailto:help.desk@utoronto.ca'>Information Commons Help Desk</a> for assistance:</p>
<p><a href='https://library.utoronto.ca/ic-help-desk-knowledge-base'>https://library.utoronto.ca/ic-help-desk-knowledge-base</a>
<br>416-978-HELP (4357)
<br>E-mail <a href='mailto:help.desk@utoronto.ca'>help.desk@utoronto.ca</a></p>
<p>Information Commons staff will assist you with resetting your UTORid password, after which you can use it to access licensed e-resources from off-campus.</p>
